<Layout title="Privacy & Your Resume Data"><main id="main" class="content-page article"><h1>Your resume data</h1><p class="lead">This page explains how this version of GlobalCV handles the information you enter.</p><h2>Guest editing</h2><p>Your current resume is kept in your browser’s session storage to help it survive a reload and the sign-in flow. It is not a saved account draft. Browsers may restore sessions; use Start a new resume to clear the current editing session on a shared device.</p><h2>Document imports and downloads</h2><p>PDF, DOCX and TXT imports are processed in your browser. The original file is not uploaded. PDF downloads are generated in your browser. Imported text becomes part of your current editing session.</p><h2>Account drafts</h2><p>When you choose Save draft, your resume is sent to the draft service and associated with your authenticated account identifier. GlobalCV stores your name, email, a salted password hash and a hashed recovery code. Raw passwords and recovery codes are not stored. An HttpOnly session cookie keeps you logged in for up to seven days. Rate-limit records help prevent repeated login attempts. Your email identifies your account; email verification and email recovery are not provided in this version.</p><h2>Deleting a draft</h2><p>Use your dashboard to delete a saved resume. This removes it from the active draft database. Downloads already saved on your device remain under your control. Hosting-provider backup retention is separate from the active database.</p><h2>Third-party resources</h2><p>The site loads interface fonts from Google Fonts. The hosting provider process the network information needed to deliver and secure the service. This version does not send resume contents to an AI service, include advertising scripts, or run session-recording analytics.</p><h2>Before advertising is enabled</h2><p>Advertising and any associated consent controls will require an updated disclosure. No active AdSense integration is included in this version.</p></main></Layout>
